coco_val2017*
val2017/
annotations/
*.pt
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pkl

# Data overrides
Dataset/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# COCO per-condition eval dump JSONs (regenerable from detections.pkl).
# Only the derived summaries and run logs are kept under version control.
# NOTE: the negation uses summary*.json (not summary.json) so per-attack
# survey outputs like summary_fgsm.json are ALSO retained.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
results_*/*.json
!results_*/summary*.json
!results_*/run.log
archive/Logs_Extra/**/*.json
!archive/Logs_Extra/**/summary*.json
!archive/Logs_Extra/**/run.log

# Future full-dataset results (N=5000 survey)
results_*_full/*.json
!results_*_full/summary*.json

# Survey resumable checkpoints / state (kept local, never committed).
# Relative patterns so they match anywhere under the repo root.
results_survey_*/checkpoint_*.pkl
results_survey_*/state_*.json
results_survey_*/*.tmp

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# results/ (consolidated layout, 2026-08-09). Same policy as the legacy
# root-level results_*/ patterns above: ignore the bulk dumps, KEEP the
# summaries, run logs and figures.
# ⚠ Do NOT write `results/*` — that excludes the sub-DIRECTORIES, and git
# cannot re-include a file whose parent dir is excluded, so every negation
# below would silently fail and all committed summaries would drop out of
# version control. Match files, not directories.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
results/**/*.json
!results/**/summary*.json
!results/**/run.log
results/**/checkpoint_*.pkl
results/**/state_*.json
results/**/*.tmp

# --smoke-test output of run_clean_control.py / run_adaptive_bpda.py: a
# plumbing check (2 images, CPU, reduced decode), never a result. Ignore the
# whole subtree so its summary*.json can never be committed by accident.
# MUST stay BELOW the !results/**/summary*.json negation — last match wins.
results/**/smoke_test/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# graphify knowledge graph (graphify-out/).
# Same policy as results_*/: track the small human-readable artifact,
# ignore the bulk-generated and machine-local parts.
#   ignored: cache/ (1.8 MB, 96 files — rebuild input, no API cost when warm)
#            graph.json + graph.html (regenerated wholesale every run)
#            manifest.json, cost.json, .graphify_python (local run state)
# DO NOT relocate the folder — "graphify-out" is hardcoded in the graphify
# package (cache.py:48, detect.py:19) and in ~/.claude/skills/graphify.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
graphify-out/*
!graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md
!graphify-out/README.md

# BFG-generated backup branches (if BFG repo cleaner is run later)
*.bfg-report/

